<title>DUBAI: Emirates signs $138 Million loan for Boeing 777.</title>
<headline>Emirates signs $138 Million loan for Boeing 777.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emirates airline on Monday signed a $138 million, 12-year loan with a consortium of banks for the sixth of seven Boeing Co 777 aircraft it has on order, the official WAM news agency reported.</p>
<p>WAM said the loan is priced on a LIBOR floating rate basis at a margin of 50 basis points.</p>
<p>The deal is led by Emirates International Bank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, the Abu Dhabi Investment Corp and other banks.</p>
<p>The Dubai-owned airline will take delivery of the aircraft in Seattle on July 25.</p>
<p>The aircraft is the third of four long-range planes to join the company this year.</p>
<p>The airline is the first carrier in the Middle East to fly this longer-range 777 model.</p>
</text>
